--TEST--
A failed conversion names a string operand by its type and its length in bytes, and never shows its text — `rule:types/single-value-types`, `rule:types/conversion`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Account {
    public string $owner = "ada";
    public int $balance = 10;
}

// A name of a million bytes gives a short message.
string $long = Core\Str::repeat("owner", 200000);
try {
    property<Account> $key = $long as property<Account>;
    echo "unreachable\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
    echo Core\Str::length($e->message) < 200 ? "short" : "long", "\n";
}

// The length counts bytes: each `€` is three bytes.
string $wide = Core\Str::repeat("a", 63) . Core\Str::repeat("€", 4);
try {
    "a"|"b" $mode = $wide as "a"|"b";
    echo "unreachable\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}

// A short operand is not shown either.
string $short = "a\nb";
try {
    "a"|"b" $other = $short as "a"|"b";
    echo "unreachable\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}

// A number that is not a whole number is not shown.
string $price = "4.5";
try {
    echo $price as int, "\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}
// covers: lang:types/property-keys
--EXPECT--
a `string` of 1000000 bytes is not one of `Account`'s public declared properties: `$balance`, `$owner`
short
a `string` of 75 bytes is not one of `"a"`, `"b"`
a `string` of 3 bytes is not one of `"a"`, `"b"`
cannot convert a `string` of 3 bytes to `int`
